    "lbs_story": {
      "type": "landing-brand-story",
      "settings": {
        "brand_story_heading": "Born in Mughal Courts. Worn by Modern Women.",
        "brand_story_text": "<p>The word <em>Anarkali</em> means <em>flower of pomegranate</em> — delicate, vivid, and impossibly beautiful. Named after a legendary courtesan of Emperor Akbar's royal court in 16th-century India, the Anarkali silhouette has graced Mughal darbaars, Bollywood screens, and the most cherished celebrations of millions of women for over 400 years.</p><p>At Janviaika, we honour that heritage while designing for the woman of today. Every piece in our collection is crafted from premium fabrics — silk, georgette, and velvet — and adorned with hand-done embroidery: zardozi, mirror work, and thread detailing that catch the light beautifully. The dramatic flared silhouette does what it has always done — it flatters every body type, creates a graceful vertical line, and makes the woman wearing it feel utterly unforgettable.</p><p>Because we believe you deserve to feel like royalty at every celebration that matters.</p>",
        "cta_link": "/collections/anarkali"
      }
    },
